# AI-Powered Customer Support & Ticket Automation Backend

A FastAPI backend for managing customer support tickets, support agents, AI-assisted replies, automation jobs, and operational analytics. Built with PostgreSQL, SQLAlchemy, Alembic, and JWT-based authentication.

> **Project status:** Backend features and Docker configuration have been developed incrementally. Before production deployment, confirm the complete test suite passes, all sensitive routes enforce authorization, and the AI automation worker is configured for reliable execution. This README describes the intended setup; some routes or filenames may differ in your checkout.

## Features

- **Customer and ticket management:** Customer records, ticket creation and updates, ticket statuses, assignment, messages, and activity history.
- **Support agents:** Agent records, activation status, administrator and agent roles.
- **Authentication:** Password hashing with Argon2, JWT login, authenticated profile, and role-based access controls.
- **AI-assisted support:** Generate draft replies; review, approve, reject, and send suggestions.
- **AI automation:** Background processing and tracking of automation jobs.
- **Analytics:** AI suggestion statistics, agent performance, and trends.
- **Database migrations:** Alembic-managed PostgreSQL schema.
- **Testing:** Pytest and FastAPI TestClient.
- **Containerization:** Dockerfile and Docker Compose for API and PostgreSQL.

## Tech stack

| Layer | Technology |
| --- | --- |
| API | Python 3.14, FastAPI, Uvicorn |
| Database | PostgreSQL 17, SQLAlchemy, psycopg |
| Migrations | Alembic |
| Authentication | PyJWT, pwdlib with Argon2 |
| AI integration | OpenAI API |
| Tests | pytest, FastAPI TestClient |
| Containers | Docker, Docker Compose |

## Prerequisites

**Local development:** Python 3.14, PostgreSQL, and a Python virtual environment.

**Docker development:** Docker Desktop with Docker Compose.

An OpenAI API key is required for functionality that calls the AI provider.

